sections.body:
`console.log(...)` writes whatever you put inside the parentheses to the **Console**. Text goes inside quotes; numbers don't:

```js
console.log("Hello, world!");
console.log(42);
console.log(3 + 4);
```

If you give several values separated by commas, they're printed with spaces in between: `console.log("Fuel:", 100)` prints `Fuel: 100`.

The `;` (semicolon) at the end of a line shows that the command is finished. It usually works without it, but writing it is a good habit.

Lines starting with `//` are **comments**: JavaScript doesn't read them; they're notes for you and your friends.

```js
// This line doesn't run, it's just a note
console.log("This line runs");
/* A comment that spans
   several lines looks like this */
```

